# model weights and caches — never commit
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.pt
*.gguf
models/
.cache/
huggingface/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# large raw outputs — keep locally, commit only summaries
results/**/*.jsonl
results/**/*.npy
results/**/*.npz
!results/**/summary*.json

# environment
.env
*.log


# vendored external research code: record the commit hash, do not re-commit the tree
third_party/llm-backdoor-scanner/
third_party/WeightWatch/
third_party/jlens/
models/

# (Path-specific un-ignore rules for the old flat results/ layout were removed on 2026-07-26 when
#  results/ was reorganised into per-experiment directories. They were already redundant -- the
#  catch-all below un-ignores every .jsonl under results/ -- and they named paths that no longer
#  exist, which would have read as live rules to the next person editing this file.)

# --- raw result data: committed deliberately --------------------------------
# Every .jsonl under results/ is committed, by explicit decision. ~57 MB total, largest single
# file 18.8 MB (results/e7/responses.jsonl) -- under GitHub's 50 MB warning and 100 MB hard limit.
# Rationale: this is a blind-audit submission whose two headline claims (E6 recovering the
# principal, E7 confirming the loyalty behaviourally) should be checkable end-to-end by a reader,
# not just via the summaries. Raw model outputs are the evidence, so they ship.
!results/**/*.jsonl
